      "writtenOn": "2025-07-14T21:08:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`PWR_SYS_RST` de-asserts `SL_S0`, at this point SOC will reset and not send any sleep notification, yet all other power signals are not changing. I can add this as a comment on code.",
      "parentUuid": "c6514418_3aa96f60",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6d4b7dd_026d21f4",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-14T23:00:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, please update the comment.\n\nIt could help readability to move these checks into a helper routine.\n```\nbool x86_mtl_can_exit_s0ix()\n    /* AP was reset... */\n    if (power_signal_get(PWR_SYS_RST))\n        return true;\n        \n    /* SLP_SO deasserted and AP sent resume command */\n    if (ap_power_sleep \u003d\u003d RESUME \u0026\u0026 power_signals_off(SLP_SO))\n        return true;\n        \n    return false;\n```",
      "parentUuid": "cacdf95e_60f3be89",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0315c228_87f5e6b3",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T17:45:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`PWR_SYS_RST` is only asserted for `sys_reset_delay`.  Does reading the `PWR_SYS_RST` in this path actually do anything?  Under what conditions would the MTL S0ix handler see `PWR_SYS_RST` asserted?",
      "parentUuid": "a6d4b7dd_026d21f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c71d5d9c_2eeeb829",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T18:25:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is in case `SYS_RST_ODL` button is pressed or `apreset` command is issued on EC terminal while on S0ix. Without this EC will not update power state.",
      "parentUuid": "0315c228_87f5e6b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d29e3008_89e7be91",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T19:46:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What triggers `x86_non_dsx_mtl_s0ix_run()` to run if `SYS_RST_ODL` changes?\nThis signal is configured as an output from EC, so I didn\u0027t think there was an ISR setup to handle it.\n\nMy concern is that you can still miss the AP reset transition because you only check `SYS_RST_ODL` during the short window when `x86_non_dsx_mtl_s0ix_run()` is called.",
      "parentUuid": "c71d5d9c_2eeeb829",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73800f63_b228ba05",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T21:39:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`PWR_SYS_RST` will not trigger anything if system is already on S0, but while on S0ix it will de-assert SLP_S0 signal, this triggers ISR to and post power sequence event to run one iteration that will be caught by `x86_non_dsx_mtl_s0ix_run`. This iteration will give a chance to read `PWR_SYS_RST`.\n\nI would not be too worried about timing, I did some experiments and SLP_S0 gets de-asserted 20 ms after asserting `PWR_SYS_RST`.",
      "parentUuid": "d29e3008_89e7be91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72f54002_3ac27a84",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-17T17:48:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the explanation.  Does it make sense to transition to S5 directly instead of S0 if `PWR_SYS_RST` is asserted?",
      "parentUuid": "73800f63_b228ba05",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9fd99655a72d7aa1bd33259a7a8e5cfbdbf75b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1268da46_25e547b5",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_mtl_pwrseq_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
